9th_Wave the samurai is booting around on the castle level
with her pet Master Lich, Babooshka (invisible, hasted master
lich, no less).
As some of you may, or may not have discovered. A master
lich pet, works in much the same manner as a master lich
non-pet. Ie: it teleports around all over the place...
bouncing from wherever you are to the up stairs and back
again. (great way to find out whereabouts the stairs are,
by the by, if you don't know).
Anyway, was walking around teh moat to map the outside of the
castle before going in (had the BoWW on) and Babooshka
pops in, and drops an unidentified wand at my feet.
Hmm... I think. The only wands I can think of that I don't
know are wishing, cancelation and nothing. On a hunch, I
zap the thing, and sure enough, its the WoW.
Seems in all his 'porting about, ol Babooshka popped into
the tower with the wand, and picked it up. Thus negatting any
need on my part to do the castle at all.
Now is it just me, or does anyone else think that the
'E' word should keep your pet from snagging items, as well
as non-pet monsters?
Just a thought.

